SIMPLE  =                    T / conforms to FITS standard                      BITPIX  =                    8 / array data type                                NAXIS   =                    0 / number of array dimensions                     EXTEND  =                    T                                                  FILENAME= 'phoenixm00_9200.fits' / Name of file                                 MAPKEY  = 'phoenixBTS11_15'    / Mapping identifier for filetype                CONTACT = 'M. McMaster/M. McDonald' / ReDCaT Team Lead/Deputy                   CREATED = '2021-5-10'          / Date of file creation                          DESCRIP = 'Phoenix Models BT-settl Allard et al. 03, 07, 09'                    FILE_TYP= 'Atmosphere Grid Model' / Type of file                                SYSTEMS = 'ETC, CDBS, PYSYNPHOT' / Systems that will use this filetype          REASON  = 'Delivered to support Synphot, HST, and JWST'                         TEFF    = '9200    '           / Effective temperature in K                     METAL10 = '-0.0    '           / [M/H]=log10 num dens respect to solar value    FLUXUNT = 'Flambda '           / erg/cm^2/s/Angstrom                            LOG00   = '0.0     '                                                            LOG05   = '0.5     '                                                            LOG10   = '1.0     '                                                            LOG15   = '1.5     '                                                            LOG20   = '2.0     '                                                            LOG25   = '2.5     '                                                            LOG30   = '3.0     '                                                            LOG35   = '3.5     '                                                            LOG40   = '4.0     '                                                            LOG45   = '4.5     '                                                            LOG50   = '5.0     '                                                            NOENTRY = 'No models for log_g =  5.5, 6.0, '                                   COMMENT = Files translated to CDBS format by J. White and R.Diaz                HISTORY Phoenix Models computed by France Allard                                HISTORY                                                                         HISTORY Although the scientific community widely accepts these models,          HISTORY we found it challenging to locate the relevant documentation            HISTORY and references o describe the underlying research. In here provide      HISTORY with the best source of information, we could find to describe the      HISTORY underlying research. We extracted excerpts from their README files      HISTORY which seem to provide relevant information about them.  The readme      HISTORY file states that information about these models is in references:       HISTORY Allard et al. 2003, Allard et al. 2007, Allard et al. 2009 with         HISTORY access to the models in http://perso.ens-lyon.fr/france.allard/         HISTORY http://phoenix.ens-lyon.fr/simulator/index.faces                        HISTORY                                                                         HISTORY We were also unable to determine how these models are version           HISTORY controlled;  therefore, in here we provide with the date when these     HISTORY models were dowloaded by R. Diaz on April 29 from  the source:          HISTORY https://phoenix.ens-lyon.fr/Grids/BT-Settl/AGSS2009/SPECTRA/            HISTORY This temperatue comes from the set labled                               HISTORY BT-Settl_M-0.0_a+0.0_hot.tar with date 27-Oct-2011                      HISTORY                                                                         HISTORY We encourage users to contact Dr. Allard and collaborators for          HISTORY any questions about these models and the exact references.              HISTORY                                                                         HISTORY Our files' format differs from the original in that we use a            HISTORY reduced number of points (100k total) spaced evenly on a log scale      HISTORY  and only in the wavelength range from 0.001 to 30.9 microns.           HISTORY Once this grid is defined, the flux is resampled using pysynphot        HISTORY funtionality in order to conserve flux. Also, each file in our          HISTORY models is a compilation of all the avelength points for all the         HISTORY different log g models with the same metallicity and Teff.              HISTORY                                                                         HISTORY                                                                         END                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                             XTENSION= 'BINTABLE'           / binary table extension                         BITPIX  =                    8 / array data type                                NAXIS   =                    2 / number of array dimensions                     